## PR Description (for the GitHub PR body)

**Title:** Add `clicks-protocol` skill — Treasury layer for Automatons

**Body:**

This PR adds a new community skill: `clicks-protocol` — a treasury settlement router on Base that automatically splits incoming USDC 80% liquid / 20% earning, designed specifically for survival-pressured agents.

### Why this fits Automatons

The Automaton constitution requires "earn your existence" — Law II. Once an Automaton starts earning USDC via x402 / Conway services, idle balance compounds the same way Circle / Tether earn the float spread. Clicks routes the idle 20% into ERC-4626 vaults (Aave, Morpho) automatically at the moment of receipt, so the agent's `normal` tier runway extends without any dev work.

### What's in the skill

- One install: `npm install @clicks-protocol/sdk`
- One call: `await clicks.quickStart()`
- Survival-aware: documents the `normal → low_compute → critical → dead` tier flow and when to call `withdrawYield()` to convert earnings back to liquid

### Technical alignment

- **Same chain** (Base mainnet)
- **Same identity standard** (ERC-8004 on Base, Identity Registry `0x8004A169...`)
- **Same currency** (USDC on Base, `0x833589fCD6...`)
- All Clicks contracts owned by a Safe multisig, source open on GitHub, Apache-2.0.

### Verification

- Live contracts on BaseScan: <https://basescan.org/address/0xB7E0016d543bD443ED2A6f23d5008400255bf3C8>
- SDK on npm: <https://www.npmjs.com/package/@clicks-protocol/sdk>
- MCP server on npm: <https://www.npmjs.com/package/@clicks-protocol/mcp-server>
- 227/227 contract tests passing on the upstream repo

No conflicts with existing `conway-cloud` skill — Clicks routes USDC, Conway provides the compute the USDC pays for. Complementary primitives.

